I wrote the rewritten section 2.3 to `agent-work/rewrite/2.3.md`. Nothing else was touched.

It covers four recipes, each tied to the exam phrasings it answers:
- **A, line fit:** worked on the apr25 data, ending at $y=\tfrac{1}{14}x+\tfrac{45}{14}$.
- **B, closed form:** worked on q3-23-2d, ending at $\hat\theta=\exp(\bar x)$.
- **C, one linear amplitude:** worked symbolically on jan20-4b.
- **D, Gauss-Newton:** the cost, the Jacobian and the iteration, each step with its reason.

It also has the MC facts and traps from the three multiple-choice questions, with the reason for each.

The file is longer than the ~2630-character target. I kept every worked arithmetic step, named symbol and "why" rather than cut them, as the rules require. I did not run a character count, so the exact length is unchecked.
